# AGENT.md — src/infrastructure/

The outermost layer. Contains all framework and I/O details.

## What lives here

- `handlers/<module>/` — Hapi request handlers (request, h). Each method
  wraps its body in try/catch and returns AppError-based responses.
- `routes/<module>/` — factories that take a pre-wired handler and return
  `ServerRoute[]`. The wiring happens in `server.ts`.
- `persistence/<module>/` — concrete repository implementations that satisfy
  the interfaces defined in `domain/`:
  - `{{moduleName}}.prisma.repository.ts` — Prisma
  - `{{moduleName}}.typeorm.repository.ts` — TypeORM
  - `{{moduleName}}.mongoose.repository.ts` — Mongoose
  - `{{moduleName}}.repository.ts` — in-memory (for `ormNone`)
  - `{{moduleName}}.orm-entity.ts` — TypeORM entity (persistence-only)
  - `{{moduleName}}.schema.ts` — Mongoose schema (persistence-only)

## Rules

- **May import from `application/` and `domain/`. Must NOT import from
  another module's infrastructure internals.**
- ORM entities and schemas are persistence details — they are NOT domain
  entities. Map between them and the domain entity in the repository.
- Handlers receive use-cases through their constructor. They never access
  repositories directly.
